    "created_at": "2025-07-18T18:35:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-18T18:35:43Z",
    "body": "Hmm, I wasnt aware of plans to change scope. I just felt scope would encapsulate what a service worker could already view/intercept since it might handle cases like using the [`Service-Worker-Allowed`](https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#service-worker-allowed) header where the scope is broader than the script URL. \n\nThat being said, I'm not very familiar with Service Workers and it seems like the Chromium implementation checks against [the scriptURL](https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/cookie_store/cookie_store.cc#246). I am happy to specify whichever seems best. ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
