    "created_at": "2025-07-21T21:02:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-21T21:02:11Z",
    "body": "https://github.com/w3c/ServiceWorker/issues/1512 is the ServiceWorker discussion on making it possible to change the scope.\n\nIt looks like [the ServiceWorkers spec explicitly sets the creation URL to the serviceWorker's script URL when setting up the SW Global Scope](https://w3c.github.io/ServiceWorker/#ref-for-dfn-script-url%E2%91%A7), so the spec may already be in agreement with the consensus here.  Would this be a situation where it would be friendly to spec-readers to add non-normative text that clarifies that for ServiceWorkers this is the script URL, since it's not directly accessible from the HTML spec which is linked to?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
